Failure Analysis Engineer

Introduction
We are seeking a Failure Analysis Engineer to join our team. The role focuses on investigating product and system failures, identifying root causes, and implementing corrective actions to improve reliability and quality across a range of products and processes.

About the Role
As a Failure Analysis Engineer, you will perform structured investigations to determine why failures occur, apply analytical methodologies, design or oversee targeted tests, review evidence, and document findings. You will collaborate with cross-functional teams to implement improvements that prevent recurrence and enhance overall performance.

Responsibilities
- Conduct failure analysis on products and components using appropriate techniques and data sources
- Develop and execute test plans to reproduce failures and validate root causes
- Interpret results, identify contributing factors, and determine root causes
- Prepare clear technical reports and present findings to stakeholders
- Collaborate with design, manufacturing, and quality teams to implement corrective actions
- Support sustaining engineering activities and design reviews
- Maintain accurate documentation and traceability of analyses

Required Skills
- Failure Analysis
- Engineering
- Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving abilities
- Data interpretation and technical reporting
- Root cause analysis
- Attention to detail and accuracy
- Effective communication and teamwork

What We Offer
- Opportunities for professional growth and development
- A collaborative, cross-functional work environment
- Exposure to challenging projects and continuous learning

How to Apply
To apply, please submit your application through the platform with a current resume and a brief description of relevant experience.
